  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Given the circle \\(x^2+y^2=25\\) and the line \\(x=3\\), what is the positional relationship between the line and the circle?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Tangent",
    "B": "Intersecting",
    "C": "Disjoint",
    "D": "The line passes through the center"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(d=3\\), \\(r=5\\), and \\(d<r\\), so the line and the circle have 2 common points.\n\nAlternative method 1: Find the common points\n\nCommon points must satisfy both equations, so substitute \\(x=3\\) into the circle equation:\n\\[\ny^2=25-3^2=16.\n\\]\nThus \\(y=4\\) or \\(y=-4\\), giving exactly two common points, \\((3,4)\\) and \\((3,-4)\\). The line and circle are intersecting, choice B.",
